  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Trans-boundary Resource Allocation Mechanisms for Peace in the Fergana Valley (stream)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">the programme has the following overall objective (oo) and specific objectives (so):..to contribute to improving the sustainable use of natural water and land resources across all riparian communities (oo1).water efficiency at the local level is improved and competition over resources reduced (so1).dialogue and cooperation between local authorities and experts at the regional level will be enhanced through mutual trust and transboundary information, platforms and dispute resolution processes (so2)..in addition, the anticipated results (r) are as follows:..an in-depth understanding of root causes (including climate stress) is developed and used to restart regional dialogue (r1).stakeholders are empowered to make nrm more conflict sensitive at the community level, while also reducing pressure on natural resources, feeding into increased regional dialogue (r2).transboundary dialogue and cooperation at the community and government level is strengthened by further improving data collection, operating infrastructure and raising awareness (r3)</narrative>
  </description>
